= Progress Report
Our project is coming along well. So far we have found some hopefully useful sources,
some of which mention our game specifically (which was quite unexpected), 
and have formed a general argument. We expect to argue that the diegetic music of _Stray_
represents the aspects of humanity preserved in the companion robots long after
humanity has perished while also conveying their robotic existence. We anticipate
spending a bit of our paper describing how diegetic music is able to represent the
world in which it exists and convey narrative. We will also spend a small portion
describing the narrative of _Stray_ in as much as it is important to our argument.
We will then look at two or three specific instances of diegetic music in _Stray_
and analyze them and how they relate to our argument.
= Division of Labor
We expect to share effort, dividing up the work as it comes up. Right now we expect
that each of us will analyze a particular instance of diegetic music in the game,
with the other sections of the paper being completed collaboratively or individually
as they come about. We also expect to complete the presentation collaboratively.
